From: OE-Alliance <oe-alliance@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: defer HiSi STB codec replacement until the old codec closes

Late H.264 extradata in TS recordings can replace the video codec. HiSi
instances share video0: preopening the replacement lets the old codec's
VIDEO_STOP/VIDEO_SELECT_SOURCE teardown disable the new decoder. Use the
existing video-thread deferred creation path for this backend only.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STB hardware backend integration]

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -136,10 +136,16 @@ bool CVideoPlayerVideo::OpenStream(CDVDStreamInfo hint)
       hint.codecOptions |= CODEC_ALLOW_FALLBACK;
     }
 
-    std::unique_ptr<CDVDVideoCodec> codec = CDVDFactoryCodec::CreateVideoCodec(hint, m_processInfo);
-    if (!codec)
+    std::unique_ptr<CDVDVideoCodec> codec;
+    // HiSi instances share one video channel. Open the replacement on the video
+    // thread after the old codec closes, or its teardown stops the new decoder.
+    if (m_processInfo.GetVideoDecoderName() != "stbplayer/hisi-dvb")
     {
-      CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CVideoPlayerVideo::OpenStream - could not open video codec");
+      codec = CDVDFactoryCodec::CreateVideoCodec(hint, m_processInfo);
+      if (!codec)
+      {
+        CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CVideoPlayerVideo::OpenStream - could not open video codec");
+      }
     }
 
     SendMessage(std::make_shared<CDVDMsgVideoCodecChange>(hint, std::move(codec)), 0);
